WEBVTT

00:01:30.950 --> 00:01:34.100
Dear viewers, do you believe in miracles?

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.820
You hit the jackpot in a lottery?!

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:40.200
<b>Group 25 
138472</b>

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:45.290
Looks like Lady Luck's finally
changed her opinion of me!

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:49.350
Now, I've decided to reward you three
for training so hard day in and day out...

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:51.500
...by treating you to whatever you want!

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:52.960
What'll it be?

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:54.720
Really?

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.130
Hmm, what should we get?

00:01:57.940 --> 00:01:58.740
Oh!

00:01:58.740 --> 00:02:02.350
I want to go out for sushi, 
but sit at the bar!

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.470
Eating at the bar...

00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.350
That's the first step to becoming an adult!

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:18.360
<b>My First Five-Star Sushi!</b>

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.640
The sushi bar...

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:26.040
A place where countless men have taken
their families and girlfriends to eat,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.390
and found a battlefield where the line
between life and death is razor thin!

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:30.880
What kind of narrative is that?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.000
<b>Sushi Alliance</b>

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:34.000
That's way more dramatic than
whatever RPG you're thinking of.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:40.430
Sushi Bar

00:02:34.310 --> 00:02:36.660
But with Lady Tsunade treating us,

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.470
we can circumvent the danger
and reach our sushi unharmed!

00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.460
Tomorrow we stuff ourselves silly!

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.060
Yahoo!

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.520
What's up, Bushy-Brows?

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.360
Sakura!

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.980
Oh, so get this...

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.960
And what of the beneficiary 
of today's miracle?

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.130
<b>Bank</b>

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:04.010
<b>138472</b>

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.830
<b>128472</b>

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:09.350
<i>I can't believe I had the wrong number!</i>

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:10.900
<i>That's so stupid!</i>

00:03:10.900 --> 00:03:12.900
<i>This isn't supposed to be a gag anime!</i>

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.270
Um, that's exactly what this is.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:21.240
<i>Then I went and promised 
to take them out to eat...</i>

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.210
I can't believe you had the wrong number.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:24.530
That's so stupid!

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.570
What a hackneyed plot.

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:29.390
Some Hokage you are.

00:03:29.390 --> 00:03:32.260
<i>I'll tarnish the title of Hokage!</i>

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.150
<i>Wait!</i>

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.150
It'd be better if we brought everyone
along and made a party of it.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.860
Let's just do conveyor belt sushi! 
Who's with me?

00:03:40.410 --> 00:03:42.580
<i>I think I can handle a conveyor belt place.</i>

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:43.420
Lady Tsunade.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:47.950
About us eating at the sushi bar.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:51.060
O-Oh, good timing.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:54.470
I think it'd be better if we brought
everyone along and made a party of it.

00:03:54.470 --> 00:03:55.180
Indeed!

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.420
So I went ahead and 
invited Naruto's group.

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.380
All of us sitting at the bar...

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.400
Whoo, let's party!

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:04.840
Yay!

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.390
Er, uh―

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.440
A cretin! I'm a brainless cretin!

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:19.890
The previous Hokages must 
be rolling in their graves!

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.750
Lady Tsunade, is everything all right?

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.700
I see.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:31.910
I promised them.
 I can't back out now.

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:34.430
I need to think of a way to trick them...

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:37.130
...without doing any more
damage to my reputation.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:41.960
Aren't they a little young to 
be sitting at the bar anyways?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:43.920
That's it, Lady Tsunade!

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.560
I've got a way to preserve 
your honor as Hokage,

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:49.630
and make them forget about
eating sushi at a five-star restaurant,

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:50.890
all at once!

00:04:51.440 --> 00:04:53.440
Leave it to me and Kakashi!

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:54.850
Huh? And Kakashi?

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.930
The day of...

00:04:56.930 --> 00:04:58.930
I can't wait.

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:01.550
<i>Well, Guy sure turned 
out to be unreliable.</i>

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.970
<i>We're just heading straight 
for the restaurant!</i>

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.780
Hold it!

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:11.740
We've heard tell that you're planning on
stuffing yourselves at a fancy sushi bar.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.600
Y-Yes...

00:05:13.600 --> 00:05:14.710
What about it?

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:18.280
You're too young to sit at the bar!

00:05:18.280 --> 00:05:19.100
Much too young!

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.390
Listen here!

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:22.600
Back during the Leaf's economic bubble,

00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.690
all the young leaf ninjas were living it up,

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:26.130
eating fancy sushi right at the bar.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:32.260
Then the bubble burst and their spendthrift ways caught up with them.

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:35.240
Wait, what economic bubble 
are you talking about?

00:05:35.240 --> 00:05:37.350
The only bubbles here are in your brain!

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:41.950
It's a war zone that swallows 
young ninjas whole!

00:05:41.950 --> 00:05:45.510
I can't believe you can 
swallow your own story.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:51.120
When you all grow up to be strong-willed ninjas,

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.040
who aren't swayed by temptation,

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.450
then, and only then, 
may you sit at the bar!

00:05:56.450 --> 00:06:01.170
Guy may be exaggerating, 
but he does have a point.

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:03.580
Not you, too, Kakashi Sensei.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.170
Perhaps we are a bit young.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:11.550
But our will is absolutely unshakable!

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:16.700
Then let's put it to the test.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:17.770
Test?

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:20.480
Okay, everyone.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:24.570
You're about to undergo the 
most grueling of tests:

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.490
Sit at the bar, order what 
you want, eat, and leave.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:31.820
Succeed, and we'll acknowledge 
you as adult ninjas.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:35.450
We just have to sit at the bar and eat?

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.430
That's right.

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:38.710
Please, this'll be a cake walk!

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.920
Yes! We'll all pass!

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.030
I'll go first.

00:06:44.030 --> 00:06:46.510
I'm going to eat that salmon 
roe no matter what!

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:49.400
Welcome!

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:52.420
Huh? What the―

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.270
You're late, Haruno.

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:56.970
Have a seat.

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:59.050
Oh, right.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:01.670
What'll it be?

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:05.020
Let's see... Squid, octopus, and gizzard shad.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.150
Same for you, miss?

00:07:07.790 --> 00:07:09.280
Go ahead.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.700
Um... sure.

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.660
Here's your squid, octopus and gizzard shad.

00:07:14.660 --> 00:07:17.370
Oh, uh, I―

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.330
Sakura!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:24.570
I get it.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:27.360
A young employee would never order...

00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:30.170
...something expensive when 
her boss was treating.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:32.930
So this what adults go through.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:35.380
If your spirit wavers,

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.630
you miss your chance to 
eat what you really want.

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:40.390
That's what it means to 
have a strong will?!

00:07:40.610 --> 00:07:42.730
Now we know what to expect.

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:45.080
I'm going on the offensive!

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:46.940
Welcome!

00:07:46.940 --> 00:07:49.030
You're late, Konohamaru.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.050
Get me some salmon roe!

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:52.660
Here ya go.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.240
Mine, mine, mine!

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:03.290
Too much wasabi!

00:08:03.290 --> 00:08:04.680
That idiot.

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:07.030
He forgot to say "hold the wasabi."

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:09.490
Being unable to handle 
wasabi is a fatal weakness.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:14.430
Being drawn into these skits 
is our fatal weakness!

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.930
Well, I've got a plan to 
get me some fatty tuna!

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:20.140
Byakugan!

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:24.530
Good idea! Now he can see 
if there's wasabi inside!

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.860
He could just ask them to hold it.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:29.250
Okay, Pops, I'll―

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:31.360
Hmm, I'd like...

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:36.130
Sea urchin, botan shrimp, your fattiest tuna, and a caterpillar roll.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:38.230
How about you, Neji honey?

00:08:38.230 --> 00:08:38.960
What?!

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.540
<i>That's the most expensive 
stuff on the menu!</i>

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:42.500
<i>It comes out to...</i>

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:45.460
What'll it be, sir?

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:47.920
Pops...

00:08:48.740 --> 00:08:49.380
Yeah?

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:53.050
A cucumber roll.

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:59.980
Ah, when your girlfriend 
suddenly orders a pricey meal,

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:03.010
you can't help but start 
obsessing over the cost,

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:05.030
and you end up ordering something 
cheap to balance it out.

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:07.650
Super-Eyebrows Sensei 
knows some scary tactics.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.760
Not as scary as Neji being 
impressionable enough...

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:12.030
...to fall for Guy Sensei 
playing his girlfriend!

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.050
That's it, I'm going.

00:09:15.050 --> 00:09:18.240
I'm a girl, so money's no object!

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:19.810
Hello!

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:21.150
Flounder, please!

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:22.960
Flounder, comin' up.

00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:24.160
Momma!

00:09:25.050 --> 00:09:27.710
I wanna try flounder!

00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:29.190
No way!

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:30.660
Kids eat kids sushi.

00:09:30.660 --> 00:09:32.760
Have an egg or salad roll.

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:35.420
One flounder.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:41.420
What?

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:48.040
Somehow I feel really bad eating this!

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:55.670
The sushi bar is riddled 
with unforeseen traps.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:09:57.950
They can set all the traps they want.

00:09:58.940 --> 00:10:02.240
If the whole counter's filled up, 
it doesn't matter!

00:10:02.650 --> 00:10:04.510
Okay, Pops, one tuna―

00:10:05.520 --> 00:10:07.920
Counter-punch!

00:10:08.470 --> 00:10:10.510
What a flawless counter-punch!

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:13.420
He just backed them into a corner...

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:15.720
Only one left.

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:19.890
Do you see now that you're 
not ready to sit at the bar?

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:24.850
<i>Maybe it is too soon for us...</i>

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:28.060
Conveyor belt sushi is plenty 
for you all right now.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:29.950
Conveyor belt sushi...

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.020
...revolves! Eureka!

00:10:32.370 --> 00:10:35.230
What'll you have, Lee?

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.400
I'd like... lean tuna, please.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:42.530
Great...

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.240
Leaf Hurricane!

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:47.900
Wh-What's he doing?

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:48.870
He's just like...

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:53.840
A sushi conveyor belt rotating 
around the interstate!

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.100
Yes.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:58.670
I just need to approach this like
I'd approach a conveyor belt place.

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:04.270
This is the way to stop 
wavering and impose my will!

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:06.600
<b>Thank you, conveyor belt sushi.</b>

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:12.070
<b>Farewell, sushi bar.</b>

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:10.270
What the heck just happened?!

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.270
And he's not saying goodbye!

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.440
Well, they got one past us.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.530
We lose.

00:11:17.730 --> 00:11:18.820
No.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:22.140
I learned something when I used
the Great Leaf Hurricane.

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:25.610
I'm more comfortable at a conveyor 
belt sushi place right now.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:29.990
I'll hold off on sitting at the
sushi bar until I'm truly an adult.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:31.130
Lee...

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:34.590
Well, I'd be happy to 
treat you all to that!

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:37.270
Yay!

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:41.040
And so, Lee and his pals swore
they'd make it to the bar someday.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:41.880
<b>Conveyor Belt Sushi</b>

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:41.880
<b>Amberjack  Salmon Roe  Lean Tuna  Medium Tuna  Fatty Tuna  Sea Urchin</b>

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.050
But...

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:47.350
Their appetites more than made 
up for the price difference.

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:51.980
Why me?

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:00.900
It's the end of another 
beautiful fall afternoon.

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.870
Guy Sensei really put us 
through the wringer today.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:07.010
What should we do now?

00:12:07.010 --> 00:12:08.200
I dunno...

00:12:08.850 --> 00:12:12.430
Enjoy the cool breeze and 
relax with a good book?

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:17.090
There's no breeze on earth cool
enough to make that relaxing!

00:12:17.530 --> 00:12:21.900
I mean, jeez, you don't have to act like
Guy Sensei when you're reading, too!

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:26.470
No, Guy Sensei is my hero, and I want
to be just like him as fast as possible―

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.140
Hey, look.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:32.140
Iruka Sensei!

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:33.810
It's been a while.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:35.730
Oh...

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.520
It's you three.

00:12:45.990 --> 00:12:49.950
<b>Friendship, Effort, and Victory!</b>

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:51.990
You can't teach?!

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:57.170
Yes... Once a week I 
teach the lower grades.

00:12:57.190 --> 00:13:00.640
Example image

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:00.630
Most of them are very spoiled,

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:03.840
refuse to listen to a word I say,

00:13:00.640 --> 00:13:04.100
Just an example

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.930
and have zero interest in 
trying to work together.

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:07.560
Seriously 
just an example

00:13:07.560 --> 00:13:10.030
Example image

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:10.010
If I scold them, they start crying,

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:13.870
and then I have to deal 
with their parents.

00:13:13.870 --> 00:13:15.260
Excuse me!

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:17.630
How dare you speak to my 
darling child like that?!

00:13:18.770 --> 00:13:22.800
Ah ha, that's what they call 
"intimidator parents," right?

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.650
So close, and yet so far...

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:27.660
There's going to be an open house.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:32.270
If I lose control of them, I'll get in trouble,

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:34.620
but I can't yell at the kids, either.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.480
Just thinking about it 
gives me a headache.

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:39.080
I see.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.520
Why don't we come in like last time,

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:46.810
and give them a hot-blooded lesson
in friendship, effort, and victory!

00:13:46.810 --> 00:13:51.600
That just looks like a lesson 
in the themes of Shonen Jump!

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:56.850
These kids have been raised 
to do whatever they please.

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.650
They couldn't care less about
friendship and effort.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:01.980
"Victory" is the only word they like.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.900
What am I going to do?

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:09.380
They don't care about 
friendship or effort...

00:14:09.870 --> 00:14:11.960
You wouldn't get along with them, Lee.

00:14:11.960 --> 00:14:15.500
But I like victory, too.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:18.170
Yeah, victory!

00:14:18.170 --> 00:14:18.750
Huh?

00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.630
The kids in this class already like
the concept of winning, right?

00:14:22.180 --> 00:14:23.930
We just need to use that...

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:27.740
...as a foundation for teaching them
the joys of teamwork, and effort!

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:33.010
I follow your logic, 
but how do we go about it?

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:34.450
Well...

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.560
Want to go ask Guy Sensei?

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:39.010
Guy Sensei...

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.480
We can use him!

00:14:42.290 --> 00:14:44.540
Then, on the day of the open house...

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:49.450
<b>Humming
Seville</b>

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.850
As I was saying, this―

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:54.300
What is going on here?

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:57.980
This lesson isn't challenging 
my smart, little sweet pea.

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.670
I'm going to the board!

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:02.130
<i>Kill me...</i>

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:04.070
What's wrong?!

00:15:04.070 --> 00:15:05.070
Iruka Sensei!

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.590
We're under attack by bad guys!

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:08.350
Bad guys?

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:11.550
Everyone stay calm!

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:17.790
Us bad guy underlings are here...

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:21.460
...to steal all your lunches!

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:24.450
We're just underlings,
but don't try and stop us!

00:15:24.450 --> 00:15:25.860
<i>How troublesome...</i>

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.050
Wait a sec...

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.000
Sensei, do something!

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:31.210
Protect my little sweet pea!

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:32.960
I'm going to the board!

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:34.060
W-W-Wait a―

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:35.360
That's enough!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:47.800
Let us, the Leaf Strawman 
Rangers, handle this!

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:50.670
The Leaf Strawman Rangers?

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.270
Let me explain.

00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:56.450
The Strawman Rangers are an 
elite squadron of warriors...

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:58.550
...who teach children the value 
of friendship and effort...

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:00.270
...in their quest for justice, and victory!

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:02.390
Why am I narrating?

00:16:02.390 --> 00:16:04.030
What are you doing?

00:16:04.030 --> 00:16:05.250
Let me explain.

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.940
Bushy-Brows asked us to 
help him with a hero skit...

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:11.540
...to teach your class the value 
of effort and friendship.

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:14.530
Why do you have to do 
a hero skit again?

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:15.680
Let me explain.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:18.120
Stop narrating!

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:20.510
<i>We use Guy Sensei!</i>

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:21.460
<i>Guy Sensei?</i>

00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:25.670
<i>We use him as our example and
become heroes like him!</i>

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:29.780
<i>It's an immutable fact that 
children look up to heroes.</i>

00:16:29.780 --> 00:16:35.300
<i>If we become heroes, they'll learn to
appreciate friendship and effort for sure!</i>

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:38.100
So leave this to us.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.560
O-Okay...

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.640
Good luck, Lee.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:44.180
Everyone transform!

00:16:44.180 --> 00:16:47.470
Show them the power of our
perfectly synchronized teamwork!

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:50.710
You're off, you're all off!

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:51.930
Transform!                 Make-up!                     Go!

00:16:50.710 --> 00:16:51.930
Change!                   Switch!

00:16:51.930 --> 00:16:54.110
Put forth some effort 
to getting in sync!

00:16:59.150 --> 00:17:00.370
Red Ranger!

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:02.370
Red Ranger!

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.370
Red Ranger!

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:06.040
On the scene!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:08.460
The one time you match 
and it's the color?!

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:10.610
I get to be red.

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:12.340
No, I do.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.080
I wanna do it!

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:17.880
It doesn't matter who's red. 
Just get on with it.

00:17:17.880 --> 00:17:19.050
Hey, Lee.

00:17:19.050 --> 00:17:21.420
Why am I pink?

00:17:22.480 --> 00:17:23.270
Why not?

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:25.740
Because it's weird, that's why!

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:27.330
Who cares?!

00:17:27.330 --> 00:17:29.920
This is our only spare costume.

00:17:33.310 --> 00:17:34.650
Red Ranger!

00:17:34.650 --> 00:17:36.560
It's all reds!

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:38.830
They all want to be the leader.

00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:40.780
They've got too much freedom!

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.890
Let me explain.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:44.120
The Strawman Rangers...

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.280
...are a group of spoiled warriors
who obtained their powers without...

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:47.620
...undergoing any trials or hardships.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.720
What kind of background is that?!

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:51.710
What happened to the 
effort and friendship?

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:53.800
This is no good.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.760
Finally, we're back on track.

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.800
We don't have a Yellow Ranger!

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.220
Not again!

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:03.750
Hey, Yellow Rangers always 
love curry, Bushy-Brows.

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:06.330
No way, I'm red.

00:18:06.330 --> 00:18:08.190
Good lord, fine...

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:11.980
Does anyone here really like curry?

00:18:11.980 --> 00:18:14.530
What is this, a public audition?!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.490
I do.

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.700
Choji, you're the bad guy!

00:18:19.350 --> 00:18:20.660
On the scene!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:22.660
Why did the enemy change sides?!

00:18:23.130 --> 00:18:24.260
Let me explain.

00:18:24.260 --> 00:18:28.600
Because the Strawman Rangers are happy
to accept random people as their friend.

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:32.630
Which totally cheapens the 
friendship between you all.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.780
This is so troublesome.

00:18:37.040 --> 00:18:38.220
Have no fear!

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:41.930
The Strawman Rangers 
will protect everyone!

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:43.280
Leave it to us!

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:46.330
You're just protecting Sakura!

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:49.640
Yeah, we gotta defend the class!

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:51.980
Then get to work!

00:18:52.340 --> 00:18:53.750
Get serious!

00:18:53.750 --> 00:18:56.530
They won't learn anything about
effort or friendship at this rate!

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:57.570
Don't worry.

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:59.790
If we fight back with teamwork,

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:03.490
the kids are sure to understand its value!

00:19:06.010 --> 00:19:08.410
You can't escape.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.830
Yeah, but now you seem 
like the bad guys!

00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:12.290
Go!

00:19:13.150 --> 00:19:15.070
Strawman...

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:17.010
Kick!

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:20.270
Troubles-argh!

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:21.680
Shikamaru, you're weak!

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:23.540
Let me explain.

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:29.410
The Strawman Rangers gang up on the
weak bad guy underlings to defeat them.

00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:31.650
That was the most pointless 
narration ever!

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:34.860
It's not over. The bad 
guys' boss must be nearby.

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.700
Oh no!

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.870
We forgot to decide who 
would play the boss!

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:45.020
What're we gonna do, Lee?!

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:46.950
Only one way out...

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:49.410
M-Me?

00:19:49.410 --> 00:19:53.080
Why is your ally suddenly 
the enemy boss?!

00:19:53.080 --> 00:19:54.500
Next time, on Strawman Rangers!

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:56.230
Betrayal, Part 1.

00:19:54.950 --> 00:19:57.340
<b>Next Time: 
Betrayal, Part 1.</b>

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.340
See you next episode!

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:58.590
You can't just end the skit now!

00:19:59.010 --> 00:20:02.180
This is getting out of hand, Bushy-Brows.

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:04.810
We're losing our audience.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:07.170
What awful lessons they're teaching!

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:09.410
This is a bad influence 
on my little sweet pea!

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:11.390
I'm absolutely going to the board!

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:16.860
<i>Please, at least teach the kids the
difference between good and evil.</i>

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:18.510
<i>Understood.</i>

00:20:18.510 --> 00:20:21.100
<i>The root of all evil...</i>

00:20:21.100 --> 00:20:23.100
<i>The source of all our problems is...</i>

00:20:23.100 --> 00:20:23.780
<i>It's...</i>

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:26.220
...you!

00:20:26.220 --> 00:20:28.990
The true bad guys, the Monster Parents!

00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:33.380
A mother who flies into 
an uncontrollable rage...

00:20:33.380 --> 00:20:35.880
...is scarier than any boss.

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:38.310
Yeah, that makes perfect sense.

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:40.170
You guys...

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:41.890
Team Super!

00:20:41.890 --> 00:20:43.430
Knock it...

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:46.440
...off!

00:20:53.470 --> 00:20:55.010
Cool!

00:20:55.010 --> 00:20:56.800
That was so cool!

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:05.220
<i>Well, it was a crazy class...</i>

00:21:05.220 --> 00:21:08.360
<i>I doubt the kids learned anything.</i>

00:21:09.170 --> 00:21:10.180
Iruka Sensei...

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:14.530
We learned something important today.

00:21:14.530 --> 00:21:16.630
We can't always let our kids run free.

00:21:16.630 --> 00:21:19.610
Sometimes, they need discipline.

00:21:20.290 --> 00:21:23.010
We were in the wrong.

00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:28.180
Ladies...

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:34.080
Setup and Punchline

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:33.050
Thus, thanks to Lee's group,

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:35.850
The students of the ninja academy 
started to like a new word.

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:39.330
In addition to "victory," 
they learned the value of...

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.740
"Punchlines!"

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:44.990
This feels wrong...

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:25.190
Next week is "Hunting for 
Matsutake Mushrooms!"

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Hunting for Matsutake Mushrooms!
Lee and Neji Part Ways!</b>

00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:27.630
and "Lee and Neji Part Ways!"

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:28.760
Part ways?

00:23:28.760 --> 00:23:30.970
I could've seen that coming.

00:23:30.970 --> 00:23:33.470
But... Lee and Neji might 
argue sometimes,

00:23:33.470 --> 00:23:35.400
but when push comes to shove,

00:23:35.400 --> 00:23:37.720
they respect each other as rivals!

00:23:37.720 --> 00:23:38.640
What did I say earlier?

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:40.410
Next time, on Strawman Rangers:

00:23:40.410 --> 00:23:41.710
Betrayal, Part 1.

00:23:41.710 --> 00:23:43.520
That was the preview?

00:23:43.520 --> 00:23:46.320
Wait, the Strawman Rangers 
aren't coming back!
